{"bio": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Vergilius was a classical Roman poet, best known for three major works\u2014the Eclogues (or Bucolics), the Georgics, and the Aeneid\u2014although several minor poems are also attributed to him. ([Source][1].)\r\n\r\n[1]: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virgil"}, "key": "/authors/OL28294A", "birth_date": "15 October 70 BCE", "type": {"key": "/type/author"}, "remote_ids": {"viaf": "8194433", "wikidata": "Q1398", "isni": "0000000121198069"}, "personal_name": "Virgil.", "death_date": "21 September 19 BCE", "photos": [3366966], "alternate_names": ["Vergilius", "P. Vergilius Maro", "P. Virgilius Maro", "Vergil", "Virgil", "Publio Maron Virgilio", "Virgile", "Virgilio", "VIRGIL.", "Publio Virgilio Maron", "Publius Virgilius Maro", "P. Vergiliua Maro", "Virgilio Publico Maron", "Virgilius Maro, Pulius, 7 or 19 B.C.", "Publius Vergelius Maro", "M. Vergilius", "Publio Virgilio Mar\u00f3n ", "Vergil.", "Vergiliu", "Virgile.", "Virgil.", "Virgil And Dryden", "Virgil Virgil", "Virgil (Publius Vergilius Maro)", "Publius Vergilius Maro Virgil", "H Rushton [translator] Virgil [ Publius Vergilius Maro ] & Fairclough", "Virgilio Publius Vergilius Maro", "Maro, Publius Vergilius ; Dryden, John (Translator, Introduction) ; Petrina, Carlotta (Illustrator)", "Theocritus Publius Vergilius Maro", "Virgil [Publius Vergilius Maro]", "Publius Vergilius Publius Vergilius Maro", "Publius Vergilius Maro (Virgil)", "publius vergilius maro"], "source_records": ["ia:virgilaeneid0000unse_t0p2", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2022-03-17", "ia:aeneislateinisch0000verg", "amazon:0342330667", "bwb:9781804172322", "bwb:9781792884153", "amazon:8490021147", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2023-04-27:P8-ART-559", "bwb:9781021411990", "promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-01-catchup:P4-ALP-757", "bwb:9781503142350", "bwb:9781985883543", "ia:diegrosserengedi0000verg"], "name": "Publius Vergilius Maro", "latest_revision": 20, "revision": 20, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value"